      "readOnly": true,
      "default": false,
      "description": "Read the voice (text to speech) and moderation settings of the Twitch alerts: whether the voice is on or muted, its voice, language, rate, pitch, volume, maximum length and whether the name is read; what each type shows and reads; the moderation choices (hold the whole alert or only hide the text, links, capital letters, repeats, number of blocked words); and the texts waiting for a decision, with their id, type, name, reason and text. The voice is the browser's: pageReport says whether the overlay page reported support and how many voices it sees.",
      "input": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "voice_moderation_update",
      "default": false,
      "description": "Change the voice and the basic moderation of the Twitch alerts. Voice: on, voice (name of a voice), language (for example en or fr), rate 0.5 to 2, pitch 0 to 2, volume 0 to 100, maxCharacters 20 to 300, readName. Moderation: holdWholeAlert (true = an alert with a refused text waits for a decision, false = it shows without the text), blockLinks, blockCaps, blockRepeats, blockedWords (list of words, any case or accent). The word list is empty by default. This is basic moderation, not a replacement for Twitch AutoMod. Nothing is sent to the screen.",
      "input": {
